 "notes": "PatchTST-lite over per-stock windows of the last 60 sessions x 14 channels (champion 10 + ['ret_1d', 'gap_pct', 'vol_z_20', 'rsi_2']), built from the parquet sorted (ticker,date); 10-session patches, stride 10 -> 6 tokens, d_model 32, 2 pre-LN layers, 4 heads, dropout 0.2 (attention-probability dropout omitted for the fused SDPA kernel), mean-pool -> logit; BCE on label_beat_mkt_20d. Train sequences capped at 60k/fold by per-date random subsampling (seed 108); all test rows kept. Early stopping on inner-val AUC (last 15% of train dates, purged 20 sessions). HALVING RULE APPLIED (spec 120k / d_model 64): the pre-run benchmark projected 164 s/epoch (>90) under box contention (load ~10-18 on 4 cores), so cap and d_model were halved; epochs unchanged. INTERPRETATION: Fails clearly: CV 0.5143 +/- 0.044 (the most dispersed model in the study), worst fold 0.4516 (April), holdout 0.4480 with a -1.9% decile spread, rank-IC NW t 0.6. The 60-session view lets it fit whatever pattern dominated the inner tail (inner-val AUC ~0.60 on the pre-break Jan-Feb tail) and that pattern inverted in April; when the pattern persisted (July 0.575) it won big. That is a regime bet, not stock selection. Run at the halved setting (60k sequences, d_model 32) because of box contention; the verdict matches the pilot's GRU/LSTM (0.489/0.502). Its score is effectively a low-vol / near-52w-high factor (per-date Spearman atr_pct -0.53, dist_52w_high +0.59): the mirror image of LambdaRank's high-vol tilt.",
